 Returns a promise that settles when the queue becomes empty.
 
+##### options
+
+Type: `object`
+
+###### signal
+
+An [`AbortSignal`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal) that can be used to cancel this wait. If the signal is already aborted, or aborts before the queue becomes empty, the promise rejects with `signal.reason`.
+
+Cancellation only affects this waiter. It does not cancel, remove, or interrupt any queued or running tasks, and does not affect other waiters.
+
+```js
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const wait = queue.onEmpty({signal: controller.signal});
+
+controller.abort(); // Only `wait` rejects
+```
+
 Can be called multiple times. Useful if you for example add additional items at a later time.
 
 > [!NOTE]
